{
  "publication_number": "US20240177057A1",
  "title": "Federated learning method and apparatus, electronic device, and storage medium",
  "assignee": "Jingdong Technology Holding Co Ltd",
  "filing_date": "2022-04-02",
  "publication_date": "2024-05-30",
  "pse": {
    "problem": "The invention addresses the limitation in traditional machine learning methods that require large amounts of labeled data to be collected, processed, and transmitted centrally for model training.",
    "solution_function": "The federated learning method performs decentralized model training by allowing clients (e.g., devices) to collaboratively update a global model by exchanging gradient information. The server coordinates the communication between clients and manages the distribution of target gradient information.",
    "solution_structure": "The electronic device includes at least one processor and memory, which stores instructions to execute federated learning-based training. The system consists of multiple client devices and a central server.",
    "solution_implementation": "Each client performs local model training on its data, calculates the gradient, and sends it to the server. The server aggregates the received gradients for the same labeled sample from different clients, determines which client owns each labeled sample, and sends the target gradients back to the corresponding client for updating their local models. This process continues until convergence or a specified number of iterations.",
    "effect": "The federated learning method reduces the need for central data collection and processing, thereby improving privacy and reducing communication costs. The distributed training can also handle a large number of devices with limited resources."
  },
